Z||000004||88formula||01-17-2001||08:27 PM||||The first thing you should do before you do anything is check the fluid level. Then you should do a fluid and filter change. To check the fluid level start the engine and put it in each gear for about 5 seconds and then return it to park. Pull the dipstick and wipe it clean. Put the dipstick back in quickly and pull it back out, the lowest reading is the fluid level. If that does not do it than you are going to have to get professional advice because automatic transmissions are complicated, especially in a Honda.<P>You should post this in the OFF Topic forum. How would it look in here if everyone started posting questions about Honda’s in here? <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||01-18-2001||09:07 AM||||I'm thinking that the torsional load is opening up a crack in the exhaust somewhere...<BR>(How would it look? It would look like not everyone only owns a Fiero, and that other cars break down.. I was hoping that I could get some help in here, since some of you seem to know a lot. It would be much more helpful than signing on to different forums for different cars...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||01-18-2001||10:07 AM||||I don't have any problem with people asking non-Fiero related questions here.  I do it myself sometime when I want to get the attention of knowledgable people that frequent this forum.<P>Can you better describe the problem you are having?  I had problems with a TH125 trans in a Pontiac 6000 that turned out to be trash shaken loose in the hydraulics from an accident.  Trans fluid conditioner eventually cleared up the problem.<P>Take care,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||01-18-2001||01:45 PM||||Well, at first I thought it was a broken exhaust somewhere... Really snarled (best word I can use.. It even sounds like the word..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But then yesterday I realized that if it's in neutral and I'm reving it, it sounds nice and quiet, but if I put it in drive, and give it the slightest bit of gas (with, or without my foot on the brake) it makes a loud snarl. Any ideas?||||reg||1
